msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-magnetometer-for-improved-performance.rst:11
#: b5d7138a3393419fa1c8cc3c4b10d763
msgid "Almost everyone has moved to :ref:`GPS+compass module <common-installing-3dr-ublox-gps-compass-module>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-magnetometer-for-improved-performance.rst:13
#: 7d820ac979d9486f92354b0cccfed90a
msgid "This page covers the installation of a stand-alone external compass ( hmc5883l-triple-axis-magnetometer).  You may alternatively use the combined :ref:`GPS+Compass module <common-installing-3dr-ublox-gps-compass-module>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-magnetometer-for-improved-performance.rst:18
#: 2791b88d9a12438cbfd5ab767ca2a2cb
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-magnetometer-for-improved-performance.rst:20
#: a81ffd94c6b445ce969528085d136989
msgid "The 3DR external compass should only be used with the APM series of autopilots, its 5 volt signal output is not compatible with Pixhawk which require 3.3 volts. For the Pixhawk use the :ref:`3DR combination GPS / Magnetometer module <common-installing-3dr-ublox-gps-compass-module>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-magnetometer-for-improved-performance.rst:27
#: 4660ee3b1162453bb59d9c9356abdc4a
msgid "If you're having trouble with magnetic noise affecting your compass on-board the APM 2.5 board, you may want to switch to an external compass that you can mount further away from noise sources such as motors and your power wiring and batteries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-magnetometer-for-improved-performance.rst:31
#: 060a2abe7b9949bda7e64ddc17789a3e
msgid "Magnetometers are most strongly influenced by DC magnetic fields and your batteries and the ESC primary power wiring are the worst offenders."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-magnetometer-for-improved-performance.rst:34
#: 34c3e550ac9b4533a3f508ed5ecc7cff
msgid "Your primary goal is to distance the magnetometer from batteries, DC battery wiring and the wiring to your ESCs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-magnetometer-for-improved-performance.rst:36
#: 12a2482f8c8840499eb68a938c3650ee
msgid "It will also help to twist the battery and ESC power and ground wires wires together where possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-magnetometer-for-improved-performance.rst:38
#: bf363a3c00bc42ed859b0e365efd4d45
msgid "It is also important to keep the magnetometer distanced from magnetic metallic objects (use nylon or non magnetic stainless screws and hardware in its vicinity and use aluminum or nylon standoffs.)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-magnetometer-for-improved-performance.rst:42
#: 34b163c122354014b90da747a03c522f
msgid "**Notes:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-magnetometer-for-improved-performance.rst:44
#: c3c0657e648c475587d67a59437a584b
msgid "If the Magnetometer board is mounted in its forward facing direction (Drone logo on the tab facing forward and in the opposite direction of the Y arrow) the (:ref:`COMPASS_ORIENT<COMPASS_ORIENT>` ) parameter will need to be set to (Normal) or \"0\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-magnetometer-for-improved-performance.rst:49
#: 757d0fb3a613499b8ce31691d7e9930c
msgid "If you have the Y arrow pointing to the front (Drone on tab pointing to the back), set (:ref:`COMPASS_ORIENT<COMPASS_ORIENT>` ) to (Yaw 180)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-magnetometer-for-improved-performance.rst:52
#: 535f06b2aa844d73a30d9fa1a9ebc405
msgid "You will need to set the Magnetometer Orientation Parameter (:ref:`COMPASS_ORIENT<COMPASS_ORIENT>` ) in the Mission Planner Advanced Parameter List correctly to accommodate the Magnetometer's orientation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-magnetometer-for-improved-performance.rst:55
#: bd5dd161a3e6441083b9b5f70f4f2418
msgid "If the Autopilot board is used in an alternate orientation (or upside down), the (:ref:`COMPASS_ORIENT<COMPASS_ORIENT>` ) parameter will need to also be adjusted to accommodate the Autopilot boards orientation as well as its own. (They are additive)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-magnetometer-for-improved-performance.rst:59
#: b9935470f4a24d5bad3cfb01fa480c7e
msgid "It can be confusing, but all orientations in 45 degree increments and even upside down can be accommodated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-magnetometer-for-improved-performance.rst:62
#: 5c53d2a060f34c34b219a24532d6a21c
msgid "This **Quick Setup Procedure** will always work and allow you to set up your compass even if you use a non-3DR magnetometer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-magnetometer-for-improved-performance.rst:64
#: 60b49ae7b127443a9c568cb1fc9645d6
msgid "Set the (:ref:`COMPASS_ORIENT<COMPASS_ORIENT>` ) **Yaw** parameter so the direction your airframe is currently pointing agrees with the **HUD** in Mission Planner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-magnetometer-for-improved-performance.rst:67
#: 5f4cbf805b3e468596eaf3c57441da29
msgid "Now turn your air frame right or left and if the compass correctly follows the direction it is pointed you are done."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-magnetometer-for-improved-performance.rst:69
#: 1b3ffeef7b2b4a1ba37c09caab1c08d3
msgid "If the compass turned in the opposite direction of your airframe set (:ref:`COMPASS_ORIENT<COMPASS_ORIENT>` ) **Roll** to **180** (flips the compass over)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-magnetometer-for-improved-performance.rst:72
#: 319d296c6cbf48bbaaa93ab91ccbcb3b
msgid "If you need to set **Roll** to **180** (:ref:`COMPASS_ORIENT<COMPASS_ORIENT>` ) will also need to include the **Yaw** from **B.** above **(Example: Yaw 180 Roll 180)**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-magnetometer-for-improved-performance.rst:77
#: c7c3e2a786b144ae8a549556e56b9f0e
msgid "Connecting to the APM 2.5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-magnetometer-for-improved-performance.rst:79
#: fb8e523413164e7ca7eeb773b91df069
msgid "**1.** Purchase an \\ *HMC5883L magnetometer breakout board*. Ensure the magnetometer board is set to use 3.3 volts (the APM 2.5’s I2C port uses 3.3 volts, not 5 volts). The magnetometer board is supplied with the 5 volt pad solder bridged and must be modified as shown below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-magnetometer-for-improved-performance.rst:87
#: d5847bec18fd4ca095f10c683b242044
msgid "**2.** Looking at the below picture, cut the jumper trace in the middle of the APM 2.5 board. This disables the SDA line to the board’s internal magnetometer, rendering it inert."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-magnetometer-for-improved-performance.rst:94
#: a538908058f84cfe81a8224694772dd6
msgid "**3.** The APM 2.5 I2C connector needs a 4 pin DF13 connector. Cut off one and and strip and tin the four wires."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-magnetometer-for-improved-performance.rst:97
#: 24b0b291db8348168dfbd2f69459b0c4
msgid "**4.** Connect the DF13’s 4 wires to the compass breakout board. Note that the wires will not be one to one. Pin 1 on the DF13 connector will not go to pin 1 of the compass board. The standard 3DR cable has one red wire and three black wires. Substitute your wire colors accordingly. Solder the wires as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-magnetometer-for-improved-performance.rst:103
#: fef10b381a3a4ddba7d6636f40ec085e
msgid "**Red wire** on end of connector (+3.3v) goes to the VCC (or +3.3v) pad on the compass board (see labels on board for location). This is the wire closest to the interior on the APM 2.5 board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-magnetometer-for-improved-performance.rst:106
#: f8ebbc39b5bf4a2baf0298541ca9b5ee
msgid "**Wire next to red wire** (SCL) goes to the SCL pad on the compass board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-magnetometer-for-improved-performance.rst:108
#: 75e2d2f234dd4744b5acd8064a0a0551
msgid "**Wire next to wire next to red wire** (SDA) goes to the SDA pad on compass board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-magnetometer-for-improved-performance.rst:110
#: 38b5511a557946c783286ede2e6468c2
msgid "**Black wire on end of connector** (ground) goes to ground pad on compass board. This is the wire closest to the edge of the APM 2.5 board."
msgstr ""

